#NEXUS

[ ji1998a_fig9: Theropod/bird cladogram, 8 tips. The root is read as a trichotomy (Velociraptorinae, Protarchaeopteryx, the rest): the Protarchaeopteryx line is aimed at the root point and only merges into the Velociraptorinae line over the last ~25 px because the two thick lines meet at a shallow angle. Read the other way, it would make (Velociraptorinae, Protarchaeopteryx) a clade. The black bars mark clades on the backbone and are not branches. Random-sample case (seed 20261106). Topology transcribed from the figure and checked at 6x; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=8;
    TAXLABELS
        Velociraptorinae
        Protarchaeopteryx
        Caudipteryx
        Archaeopteryx
        Mononykus
        Shuvuuia
        Enantiornithes
        Ornithurae
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE ji1998a_fig9 = [&R] (Velociraptorinae,Protarchaeopteryx,(Caudipteryx,(Archaeopteryx,((Mononykus,Shuvuuia),(Enantiornithes,Ornithurae)))));
END;
